.TH ORO-CREDENTIALS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:credentials \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:credentials'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Explicit Android 14+ or Linux Secret Service password selection. Enable `[credentials] enabled = true`. WebView Autofill, passkeys and account/server authorization remain separate. iOS/iPadOS, macOS and Windows explicit\-selection backends are not implemented. `getStatus()` reports unavailable with a reason; selection rejects ENOSYS on missing backends. Android also requires an eligible installed password provider; Linux requires a running unlocked Secret Service and interactive session.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetStatus()\fR
Queries support without opening a provider or reading a credential. Missing or platform\-restricted backends return unavailable status; operational calls still reject with ENOSYS.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<PasswordSelectionStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBselectPassword(options)\fR
Opens the native provider chooser after an explicit user action. Results bind to the requesting foreground document and are never persisted or logged by this API. No remote origin is asserted; providers determine app association. It does not submit a form, save/update a password or authenticate a server. Cancellation rejects ABORT_ERR; no available credential rejects ENOENT. A provider result waits at most five seconds for the requesting Activity to resume, then revalidates document ownership and the foreground window. Cancellation, navigation, activity stop and the original deadline still apply. Linux shows at most 64 matching Secret Service accounts in a native modal. Items must carry `application=<bundle identifier>` and `username` attributes. Only the chosen item is unlocked/read. These lookup attributes are not an attested app association. Secret Service providers and locked\-keyring prompts require desktop qualification; no browser\-origin association or automatic fill is added.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (PasswordSelectionOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<SelectedPassword>\fR
